  "reviewer": "visual-agent",
  "notes": "Opened selection.frame.png (1800x900, first plate frame) and prompts/kf_00000.png at 1x, 2x, 4x and 5x with the mask contour drawn on the raw pixels. The BiRefNet mask swallowed both wings of the black gaming-chair backrest, which is the same black as his cap and t-shirt: chair included from y~255 down to the shoulders, left wing x 641-700 and right wing x 1018-1072. Wrote two exclude polygons that follow the chair only, held 6-12 px clear of him at every sampled row: cap crown/brim untouched, both ears kept whole (his right ear outer edge x~683 vs cut at x 674; his left ear outer edge x~1016 vs cut at x 1026-1030), jaw and beard edge kept at x 690-710 left and 985-1012 right, neck kept, and the polygon bottoms ride 8 px above the measured t-shirt shoulder diagonal on each side (left shoulder top y~535 at x 640 rising to y~517 at x 708; right shoulder top y~512 at x 990 falling to y~548 at x 1060). Re-rendered the corrected mask and inspected it tinted and as a contour: chair now black on both sides, cap, ears, jaw, neck, shoulders, torso and both blurred hands still inside. Mask coverage 0.2973 -> 0.2810, consistent with removing the two chair wings only. Coordinates measured on this frame; nothing carried from another recording.",
